#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Mobipick voice agent: talk to the robot through the OpenAI Realtime API.

An optional front end to the mobipick_gpt agents, replacing speech
recognition + TTS. Everything the agents say on /speak (and anything
published on /realtime/say) is spoken verbatim in the realtime voice, with
the robot's own voice cancelled from the microphone. Two modes:

  bridge (default)  a pure speech bridge: the robot reads an order back
                    ("Pick the Pringles?") and on a yes it goes verbatim to
                    /recognized_speech, where the mobipick_gpt router,
                    chatbot and planner decide what to do and what to
                    answer. "stop" and "cancel" go out at once. The confirmation
                    keeps words the transcription invents from noise away
                    from the robot (--no-confirm skips it). The realtime
                    model never replies on its own; it only speaks /speak.
  agent             the realtime model is Mobipick's persona
                    (mobipick_gpt/config/prompts/realtime_voice.txt): it
                    answers small talk itself and calls "execute" for orders
                    and live-state questions.

In both modes, while an order runs every utterance also reaches it as an
event (check_for_events(), listen()).

ROS is reached over rosbridge (roslibpy), so this runs where the microphone
and speaker are, e.g. on the host next to the Mobipick containers.

Topics
  publishes   /recognized_speech            std_msgs/String  tasks, questions, answers -> mobipick_gpt
              /realtime/user_transcript     std_msgs/String  what the person said
              /realtime/robot_transcript    std_msgs/String  what the robot said
              /realtime/is_speaking         std_msgs/Bool    robot voice active
              /realtime/mic_ok              std_msgs/Bool    false: the mic delivers only digital silence (muted)
  subscribes  /speak                        std_msgs/String  said verbatim (mobipick_gpt output)
              /realtime/say                 std_msgs/String  said verbatim (anything else)
              /mobipick_gpt/gpt_debug       std_msgs/String  action progress, kept as silent context
              /mobipick_gpt/busy            std_msgs/Bool    a task runs: every utterance goes out as an event
              /realtime/talk                std_msgs/Bool    --push-to-talk: true opens the mic, false closes it

Examples
  realtime_voice_agent                                  # host defaults: rosbridge ws://localhost:9090, LiteLLM :4000
  realtime_voice_agent --voice echo --input ALU1 --output Pebble
  realtime_voice_agent --push-to-talk                   # public demo: only the operator is heard (scripts/push_to_talk)
  rostopic pub -1 /realtime/say std_msgs/String "data: 'Hello, I am Mobipick.'"
"""

